# Per-project cloud identity for RIVR.
#
# THE RULE THIS ENFORCES: RIVR's Firebase and GCP account is
# jersondevs@gmail.com, never admin@oqupa.com. Getting that wrong has already
# cost real time, and a deploy under the wrong account is not something you
# notice until afterwards.
#
# Jerson works on Oqupa constantly, so switching the GLOBAL gcloud account is
# not an option. gcloud has no per-directory concept of its own, but it does
# have named configurations, and CLOUDSDK_ACTIVE_CONFIG_NAME selects one for
# the current shell only. direnv exports it on entering this directory and
# unsets it on leaving, so nothing outside RIVR is affected.
#
# The `rivr` configuration holds account=jersondevs@gmail.com and
# project=ciroh-rivr-app. The `default` and `oqupa` configurations are
# untouched and still resolve to admin@oqupa.com.
#
# The Firebase CLI needs nothing here: it already stores the account per
# project directory (`activeAccounts` in its configstore), and this directory
# is already mapped to jersondevs@gmail.com. Verified by running
# `firebase login:list` from here and from home and getting different answers.
#
# If this ever stops taking effect, the usual cause is that direnv has not
# been granted permission for this directory. Run `direnv allow` here.
export CLOUDSDK_ACTIVE_CONFIG_NAME=rivr
